# Digital Libraries: Situating Use in Changing Information Infrastructure.

**Authors:** Bishop, Ann Peterson, Neumann, Laura J., Star, Susan Leigh, Merkel, Cecelia, Ignacio, Emily, Sandusky, Robert J.

## Abstract
Reviews empirical studies about how digital libraries evolve for use in scientific and technical work based on the Digital Libraries Initiative (DLI) at the University of Illinois. Discusses how users meet infrastructure and document disaggregation; describes use of the DLI testbed of full text journal articles; and explains research methodology. (Contains 67 references.) (LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ605300

